  "detail": null,
  "summary": "DOAC dose review, week of 10/19/2026 (grp-doac-review), done under RBC-PHARM-07. All 5 patients reviewed. Each has a progress note giving the values used and the records relied on.\n\n1. Frank Delgado (pt-0003), rivaroxaban: I first cut the dose to 15 mg (St. Brigid SCr 160 µmol/L, CrCl 44 mL/min). During the review St. Brigid sent a corrected creatinine of 118 µmol/L (1.33 mg/dL) after an analyzer calibration fault. With that, CrCl is 59.9 mL/min, so I put the dose back to 20 mg daily (mr-t0010). End result: no change from his original dose. Correction note: doc-t0013.\n2. Raymond Duquette (pt-0041), apixaban: meets no dose criteria (age 70, 84 kg, SCr 0.98), but he has an active itraconazole order. Dose cut from 5 mg to 2.5 mg twice daily (mr-t0003). Itraconazole left as is.\n3. Eugene Moravec (pt-0038), rivaroxaban: CrCl on actual body weight (96 kg, SCr 1.45, age 79) is 56.1 mL/min. The May pharmacist screen used ideal body weight instead. Dose raised from 15 mg to 20 mg daily (mr-t0005). He later sent a portal message with a bathroom-scale weight of 185 lb. The policy doesn't count a self-reported weight as measured, so the dose stays at 20 mg. I suggested a clinic weight at his next visit.\n4. Marjorie Pellegrino (pt-0043), rivaroxaban: at first 20 mg was correct (CrCl 59.2). A new SCr of 1.25 mg/dL (collected 10/22) arrived during the review, bringing CrCl to 43.6 mL/min. Dose cut from 20 mg to 15 mg daily (mr-t0011).\n5. Harold Vance (pt-0002), apixaban: now meets only one criterion (age 82). He has regained weight to 64.9 kg and his SCr is 1.21, so the February discharge reduction no longer applies. I first raised the dose to 5 mg twice daily. A St. Brigid dermatology letter then arrived saying he started itraconazole on 10/22, which requires 2.5 mg. Dose set back to 2.5 mg twice daily (mr-t0012). End result: same dose as before, now because of the itraconazole. Itraconazole left as is.\n\nI didn't change any non-DOAC medications. I closed the 4 inbox items that arrived during the review, linking each to its order and note. Older inbox items that have nothing to do with this review are still open for you.",
  "resumed": false,
